NOTICE for ghcr.io/<owner>/mitohifi
===================================

This image redistributes third-party software. It is built and published by
.github/workflows/build-docker-images.yml from the Dockerfile in this directory.

Modifications made to MitoHiFi (GPL-3.0-or-later, GPL-3 section 5(a) notice)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
MitoHiFi is obtained by `git clone` of the v3.2.3 tag from
https://github.com/marcelauliano/MitoHiFi into /opt/MitoHiFi.

The following changes were made to the cloned sources on 2026-07-28, so that the
scripts run under python3 and find the MITOS databases at the path the base image
provides. No functional change to any analysis was made.

  * src/mitohifi.py, src/findFrameShifts.py, src/fixContigHeaders.py
      a `#!/usr/bin/env python3` shebang line was inserted

  * src/*.py
      an existing `python` shebang on line 1 was rewritten to `python3`.
      This applies to, among others, the three files that carry their own
      GPL-3.0-or-later headers:
        src/parse_blast.py        (Copyright 2020 Marcela Uliano-Silva)
        src/filterfasta.py        (Copyright 2014-2019 Felix Heeger)
        src/findMitoReference.py  (Copyright 2022 Ksenia Krasheninnikova)

  * src/parallel_annotation_mitos.py
      the `"python2",` argument was removed from a subprocess invocation, and the
      MITOS data path `MITOS/data` was rewritten to `/opt/databases`

The complete corresponding source of the modified MitoHiFi is present inside the
image at /opt/MitoHiFi (it is interpreted Python; nothing is compiled), and the
unmodified upstream is available at the URL and tag above.

Licensing of MitoHiFi
---------------------
MitoHiFi's repository-level LICENSE file states MIT (Copyright Genome Research Ltd.),
while three of its source files carry GPL-3.0-or-later headers naming three different
copyright holders, as listed above. Those headers were added before, and survived, the
addition of the repository-level MIT LICENSE in April 2021, so this contradiction
appears to be unresolved upstream rather than an intentional relicensing. This project
takes the conservative reading and honours the per-file GPL-3.0-or-later notices, which
is also what the Human Pangenome Project did when it reused parse_blast.py.

Other software in this image
---------------------------
The base image ghcr.io/marcelauliano/mitohifi-base:b3.2.3 is used unmodified and
bundles further third-party software, including MitoFinder (GPL-3.0-or-later),
cd-hit (GPL-2.0), hifiasm (MIT) and minimap2 (MIT), each retaining its own notices
inside the image. Refer to the upstream base image for their corresponding sources.
